structured-zstd 0.0.58: the encoder wrote Number_of_Sequences wrong from 0x7F00 sequences in a
block on (RFC 8878 3.1.1.3.2.1): the two-byte form reached 0x7FFF, whose first byte, 255, the
decoder reads as the long form; and the long form's 16-bit value went out big-endian. Blocks
with that many sequences come from the optimal parser (levels 16+, three-byte matches) on
repetitive input, e.g. seq 1 300000 | zstd -19: the frame did not decode (C zstd: Data
corruption detected).

--- a/src/encoding/blocks/compressed.rs
+++ b/src/encoding/blocks/compressed.rs
@@ -2902,23 +2902,26 @@
     }
 }
 
+/// Number_of_Sequences (RFC 8878 3.1.1.3.2.1): one byte below 128; two bytes, the first
+/// 128 + (n >> 8), up to 0x7EFF (a first byte of 255 means the long form); else 255 and
+/// n - 0x7F00 as a little-endian 16-bit value.
 fn encode_seqnum(seqnum: usize, writer: &mut BitWriter<impl AsMut<Vec<u8>>>) {
     const UPPER_LIMIT: usize = 0xFFFF + 0x7F00;
     match seqnum {
         1..=127 => writer.write_bits(seqnum as u32, 8),
-        128..=0x7FFF => {
+        128..=0x7EFF => {
             let upper = ((seqnum >> 8) | 0x80) as u8;
             let lower = seqnum as u8;
             writer.write_bits(upper, 8);
             writer.write_bits(lower, 8);
         }
-        0x8000..=UPPER_LIMIT => {
+        0x7F00..=UPPER_LIMIT => {
             let encode = seqnum - 0x7F00;
             let upper = (encode >> 8) as u8;
             let lower = encode as u8;
             writer.write_bits(255u8, 8);
-            writer.write_bits(upper, 8);
             writer.write_bits(lower, 8);
+            writer.write_bits(upper, 8);
         }
         _ => unreachable!(),
     }
